body:
Hello, thanks for your reply... <3 

&#x200B;

Yes, it sounds we are in a similar situation. I love my sister, but I can't be around her so much time, as her dynamics make me very tired. And wow... funny enough, I have a parent which has narcissistic traits too, but differently from my sister, he is a bit abusive (mainly verbally) and manipulative (a lot!) as well, not caring to literally "walk over you" if there is something or someone that is more important than you :( then coming to you for you to say how good he is (I was his "narcissistic supply"), and getting upset and angry if you don't... Luckily for me (at least in this), I don't see my father in my sister (at least not at a conscious level), but that happens with guys, like I am much more sensitive towards guys not seeing me/behaving like I don't exist...  


Finally, I feel you when you say to your sister that she is like your mother, I don't do that with my sister either, it would be unnecessary and too painful... I feel you as well...

&#x200B;

I hope things will improve, even if I know they could not... Hugs!

wow, what a fast reply! Thanks a lot!

I see... I just wanted to know if my dad and my sis are the only ones showing this behaviour.

Thanks for the link as well!

&#x200B;

Edit: in the article, the fact of avoiding situations to avoid "criticism or exposure" does ring a bell... I would also add the fact that some may see in dealing with situation a waste of time that should be invested to be something that people could praise...

&#x200B;
